{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But if he stands a day or two days, he shall not be avenged, for he is his money.</b> Not just one day — even two days. For you might have thought: since he stood two days and died on the third day, surely he died on account of his wound, for a wound hurts most on the third day, as it is written (Genesis 34:25) ״וַיְהִי בַיּוֹם הַשְּׁלִישִׁי בִּהְיוֹתָם כֹּאֲבִים״ — therefore it teaches us 'יוֹמַיִם,' for whether one day or two days, we suspend judgment and say that he died on account of some other thing that newly befell him. And he certainly did not strike him a cruel blow sufficient to kill, 'for he is his money' — and would you have a man who destroys his own money with his own hands? Surely he did not strike him a great blow, for he was sparing of his property, and he died on account of something else."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:22:20.485520399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}